### Problem Statement
Paper includes an in-memory HTTP + SSE collaboration relay in `app/collaboration/server.ts` that handles real-time multiplayer editing, cursors, and presence. While this is used by the Vite dev/preview plugin, it was never mounted into the production Docker Fastify backend (`app/server/index.ts` / `service.ts`). Furthermore, `docker/nginx.conf` lacks a location block for `/__paper_collaboration/`, causing all collaboration requests in production to fall through to `index.html` and return `405 Method Not Allowed`.

### Requirements & Scope (Phase 2 - Priority 2)
1. **Mount Relay in Fastify / Backend Service:**
   - Mount `CollaborationServer` in `app/server/` to handle all `/__paper_collaboration/*` requests:
     - `POST /__paper_collaboration/:room/join`
     - `GET /__paper_collaboration/:room/events` (SSE streaming)
     - `POST /__paper_collaboration/:room/update`
     - `POST /__paper_collaboration/:room/leave`
   - Update `app/tsconfig.server.json` if needed to ensure collaboration server files compile into `server/dist`.
2. **Reverse Proxy Configuration in Nginx:**
   - In `docker/nginx.conf`, add:
     ```nginx
     location /__paper_collaboration/ {
         proxy_pass http://paper-api:3001;
         proxy_http_version 1.1;
         proxy_set_header Host $host;
         proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
         proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
         proxy_buffering off;
         proxy_cache off;
         proxy_read_timeout 3600s;
         proxy_send_timeout 3600s;
         client_max_body_size 17m;
     }
     ```
3. **Verification:**
   - Test that `POST /__paper_collaboration/<room>/join` returns `200 OK` with session credentials and registers.
   - Test that `GET /__paper_collaboration/<room>/events` opens an active SSE stream.
   - Run `npm run build` and `npm test` (including `collaboration.test.mjs`).

Reference: Closes #14
